# Project board status on every PR

The backlog lives on [Design System DudaX](https://github.com/orgs/dudaloglobal/projects/2). On every PR create or update, move linked issues to the matching Status. Do not leave completed work in Backlog.

## Keywords in the PR body

- `Closes #N` — work for that issue is done in this PR.
- `Related to #N` — work started but the issue is not finished.

Branch name `feature/DS-XXX-…` is a hint, not a close.

## Status mapping

| PR state | `Closes #N` | `Related to #N` |
|---|---|---|
| Draft | En cours | En cours |
| Open, ready for review | En revue | En cours |
| Merged | Terminé (issue closes via `Closes`) | En cours |
| Closed without merge | En cours | En cours |

Unstarted issues stay in Backlog.

## How

1. Put `Closes #N` / `Related to #N` in the Ticket section (never only “Related to” for finished work).
2. Run `.github/scripts/sync-project-status.sh <pr-number>` after `gh pr create` or `gh pr edit`.
3. CI workflow `.github/workflows/project-status.yml` does the same when secret `PROJECT_TOKEN` is set. Without that secret the job is skipped and does not fail the PR.
4. Strip any tooling attribution from the PR body.

Do not add Co-authored-by or tooling attribution.
